# ShipSafe local configuration — example only.
#
# Copy to `.env` in the repository root. `.env` is git-ignored.
# `python scripts/dev.py` reads SHIPSAFE_* lines from `.env`; if you start
# uvicorn yourself, export the variables in your shell instead.
# Every variable is optional, and ShipSafe needs no secret to run. The only
# secrets are SHIPSAFE_BITBUCKET_TOKEN, SHIPSAFE_GEMINI_API_KEY and SHIPSAFE_OPENAI_API_KEY,
# used when you turn Bitbucket, Gemini or OpenAI on. Full reference: docs/CONFIGURATION.md

# Extra directory whose Git repositories may be scanned, in addition to the
# synthetic demo repository (which is always allowed). Unset = demo only.
# Must be a specific, approved workspace directory; a drive or filesystem
# root is refused at startup.
# SHIPSAFE_ALLOWED_ROOT=C:\work\approved-repos

# SQLite file for scan history and imported reviews.
# Default: backend/.shipsafe-data/scans.db
# SHIPSAFE_DB_PATH=

# Where the synthetic LedgerLite demo repository is generated. It is always
# scannable, so like SHIPSAFE_ALLOWED_ROOT it must not be a drive or
# filesystem root. Must be empty, absent, or the previously generated demo.
# Default: backend/demo-repo
# SHIPSAFE_DEMO_DIR=

# Frontend only (read by Vite at build/dev time, put it in frontend/.env.local):
# base URL of the API. Leave unset to use the dev-server /api proxy.
# VITE_API_BASE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bitbucket Cloud (optional, read-only). Leave all four unset to keep
# Bitbucket off. Set WORKSPACE, REPOSITORIES and TOKEN together: a partial
# configuration stops the API at startup. The /api/bitbucket/* routes use
# these settings, and so do the dashboard's Bitbucket screens.
#
# The token is a SECRET. Keep it only in your local `.env` (git-ignored) or an
# approved secret store. Never commit it, paste it into a chat or prompt, or
# put it in a VITE_* variable. Give it read access to repositories and pull
# requests only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Workspace slug, as in https://bitbucket.org/<workspace>/
# SHIPSAFE_BITBUCKET_WORKSPACE=

# Comma-separated repository slugs ShipSafe may read. Nothing else in the
# workspace is reachable.
# SHIPSAFE_BITBUCKET_REPOSITORIES=repo-one,repo-two

# Access token (sent as Bearer), or an Atlassian API token when
# SHIPSAFE_BITBUCKET_EMAIL is also set (sent as Basic auth).
# SHIPSAFE_BITBUCKET_TOKEN=

# Optional. Atlassian account e-mail; set it only with a scoped API token.
# SHIPSAFE_BITBUCKET_EMAIL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini AI review (optional). The API server sends a scan's secret-redacted
# diffs to Google Gemini and stores the answer as an UNVERIFIED AI review.
# Non-demo code is sent only after the person confirms sharing for that scan.
#
# The key is a SECRET: local `.env` or an approved secret store only. Never
# commit it, paste it into a chat or prompt, or put it in a VITE_* variable.
# Its Google project must have Gemini API access (billing may be required).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SHIPSAFE_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Default: gemini-flash-latest
# SHIPSAFE_GEMINI_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI AI review (optional). Same rules as Gemini above: the API server sends
# a scan's secret-redacted diffs to OpenAI and stores the answer as an
# UNVERIFIED AI review; non-demo code only after the person confirms sharing.
#
# The key is a SECRET: local `.env` or an approved secret store only. Never
# commit it, paste it into a chat or prompt, or put it in a VITE_* variable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SHIPSAFE_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Default: gpt-6-luna
# SHIPSAFE_OPENAI_MODEL=

# Optional. minimal | low (default) | medium | high | none
# SHIPSAFE_OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=
